From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: ingenic: accept the QEMU T41 XBurst2 processor ID

The kernel never reaches the console: cpu_probe_ingenic() panics with
"Unknown Ingenic Processor ID!" before arch_mem_init() parses the
command line and brings up the early console, so the panic is only
visible in the printk ring buffer.

The Ingenic QEMU fork's ingenic-t41 machine runs a core it calls
"XBurst2-MXU3.1" (target/mips/cpu-defs.c.inc, branch ingenic-txx),
reporting PRID 0x00132100: PRID_COMP_INGENIC_13 with IMP 0x2100.
Mainline names only the 0x2000 IMP for XBurst2, so the probe takes the
default arm. Measured on a booted image as well: the processor_id field
of current_cpu_data in guest RAM holds 0x00132100.

Accept the modelled IMP as the same core. Confirm the value against
real T41 silicon when one is on the bench.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/cpu.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/cpu.h
@@ -191,6 +191,13 @@
 #define PRID_IMP_XBURST2		0x2000	/* XBurst®2 with MXU2.1 SIMD ISA		*/
 
 /*
+ * The XBurst2 core as the Ingenic QEMU fork models it (machine
+ * ingenic-t41, cpu XBurst2-MXU3.1): COMP 0x13, IMP 0x2100, so PRID
+ * reads 0x00132100. Mainline only names the 0x2000 IMP for XBurst2.
+ */
+#define PRID_IMP_XBURST2_QEMU	0x2100	/* XBurst2 core as modelled by qemu-ingenic */
+
+/*
  * These are the PRID's for when 23:16 == PRID_COMP_NETLOGIC
  */
 #define PRID_IMP_NETLOGIC_XLR732	0x0000
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
@@ -1823,6 +1823,7 @@
 		break;
 
 	/* XBurst®2 with MXU2.1 SIMD ISA */
+	case PRID_IMP_XBURST2_QEMU:
 	case PRID_IMP_XBURST2:
 		c->cputype = CPU_XBURST;
 		__cpu_name[cpu] = "Ingenic XBurst II";
